--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/1135-sinker-template-library.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+## #1135 - the empty sinker template joins the machine library
+
+**Decided.** `assets/machines/sinker-edm.mch` ships in `posting::MACHINES`
+as "Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)". Its `edm` section stays empty. The
+sinker post "Sinker EDM (ISO)" is its only post.
+
+**Why.** Every library machine needs a post. The post shipped with #542.
+The user fills the codes from the control manual, and the post refuses by
+name until then.
+
+**Dropped.** Moving the test fixture (`crates/app/tests/edm/sinker-edm.mch`)
+into the assets: about a dozen suites include it by path. The fixture stays
+as a copy, and a test pins that it equals the shipped file. The wire
+template stays a fixture: no issue asked for it.
+
+**Cost to change.** Rename the picker label in one line of `posting.rs`.

From 0c477509a52eb9b8ac5268e00cd7c97d09b097c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:21:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(ui): ribbon mode row for the sinker EDM template

Main (issue 1501) added the MACHINE_MODES table and a guard test: every
machine kind in the built-in library has a ribbon mode row. This PR is
the first to ship a SinkerEdm machine, so the guard failed after the
merge of main.

Add a "Sinker EDM" row that mounts "Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)" through
the same undoable LoadBuiltinMachine as the other rows, and the door word
"Sinker". The guard stays as it is. The template post still refuses by
name until edm.codes is filled in (pinned by
sinker_burn::the_shipped_sinker_template_lists_and_refuses_its_unfilled_codes_by_name).
The short_caption wildcard arm is removed: every kind now has an arm.

Tests: machine_mode_tests asserts the sinker row; tips_match_the_imgui_table
takes the new door tip. Decision recorded in
docs/decisions/1135-sinker-template-library.md.

Refs #1135

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
